				\begin{document}$$550^\circ$$\end{document} C. This includes comparing intragranular orientation changes via grain reference orientation deviation (GROD). Additionally, this study compares CPFE elastic strain results to experimentally determined elastic strains in an effort to validate the proposed CPFE model. Improving results of modelling by including more information, in this case 3D microstructure, may seem intuitive; however, this does not mean it is inherently true. This work is designed to provide some evidence for this intuition. Additionally, if 2D microstructural representations allow for sufficient reproduction of mechanical behaviour, then this would greatly simplify the experimental data required. The paper starts by introducing the experimental methods and subsequent data analysis procedures used in section “ Methods ”. These include in situ HR-EBSD, HR-EBSD elastic strain measurements via Kikuchi patterns, and 3D EBSD. Section “ Crystal plasticity model ” outlines the mathematical basis of the crystal plasticity model used and well as the calibration of the model. Section “ CPFE model geometries and boundary conditions ” describes the microstructural model geometries and boundary conditions applied. 3D EBSD data are used to reconstruct a full microstructure alongside a oligocrystal geometry. Section “ Results ” presents the results, comparing the 3D EBSD, oligocrystal, and experimental results. Section “ Discussion ” discusses these results, and finally, Section “ Conclusions ” presents the conclusions.

